# The build context is sent to the daemon before anything is built, so shipping data/
# wholesale would push ~90 GB across a socket to produce a ~700 MB image.
#
# The heavy directories are named one by one rather than excluding `data/` and
# re-including `data/curated_data/demo_cases/`. Docker does support that, but the
# semantics of re-including a path under an excluded parent are subtle enough that a
# mistake shows up as a COPY failure at build time. Naming what to exclude cannot
# fail that way, and the demo cases are what make the image work at all.
data/raw_data/
data/preprocessed_data/
data/curated_data/slice_bank_p2/
data/_legacy/
models/dbt/
models/tabular/
models/_legacy/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.kaggle/

logs/
plots/
reports/
tests/
scripts/
pipelines/
*.ipynb

*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
.gitignore
